# Handle Overdispersed Counts with Negative Binomial

Count data often violates the Poisson assumption that the variance equals the mean. When the
observed variance is substantially larger (a condition called overdispersion) a Poisson GAM
underestimates uncertainty and produces confidence intervals that are too narrow. The Negative
Binomial family adds a dispersion parameter that absorbs the extra variation, giving honest standard
errors and better-calibrated predictions.

## Load data

Load the fish dataset and inspect it.

::: {#5b72e97a .cell execution_count=1}
``` {.python .cell-code}
import whittaker as wk

data = wk.load_dataset("fish", as_frame=True)
data.columns.tolist()
```

